1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,406
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:02,909 --> 00:00:05,188
Oops, my bad—I totally forgot!

3
00:00:05,412 --> 00:00:07,644
But I think you'll find it interesting!

4
00:00:07,644 --> 00:00:09,644
Come on, stay with me here!

5
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: The Basics of Customer Service

6
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,379
Excuse me.

7
00:00:13,402 --> 00:00:16,070
Welcome! How can I help you?

8
00:00:16,094 --> 00:00:19,294
Could I see this shirt, please?

9
00:00:19,317 --> 00:00:21,888
Of course, here you go.

10
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:23,879
Thank you.

11
00:00:23,902 --> 00:00:26,556
This looks really nice.

12
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:30,380
Yes, it's very popular.

13
00:00:30,403 --> 00:00:32,822
How much is it?

14
00:00:32,845 --> 00:00:35,135
It's 3,000 yen.

15
00:00:35,159 --> 00:00:36,844
I see.

16
00:00:36,867 --> 00:00:39,685
Do you have other colors?

17
00:00:39,709 --> 00:00:43,189
Yes, we have white and black.

18
00:00:43,212 --> 00:00:45,685
Could I see the white one, please?

19
00:00:45,709 --> 00:00:48,328
Sure, here it is.

20
00:00:48,351 --> 00:00:50,327
It's beautiful.

21
00:00:50,351 --> 00:00:53,385
What size is this?

22
00:00:53,409 --> 00:00:55,548
It's a medium.

23
00:00:55,572 --> 00:00:58,105
Do you have a large size?

24
00:00:58,128 --> 00:01:00,528
Yes, we do.

25
00:01:00,551 --> 00:01:03,151
Just a moment, please.

26
00:01:03,174 --> 00:01:04,780
Thank you.

27
00:01:04,803 --> 00:01:06,770
Sorry to keep you waiting.

28
00:01:06,793 --> 00:01:08,834
Here's the large size.

29
00:01:08,857 --> 00:01:11,224
May I try it on?

30
00:01:11,247 --> 00:01:14,425
Of course, the fitting room is over there.

31
00:01:14,448 --> 00:01:16,315
Thank you.

32
00:01:16,338 --> 00:01:18,225
How does it look?

33
00:01:18,248 --> 00:01:20,539
It fits perfectly.

34
00:01:20,562 --> 00:01:22,796
It really suits you!

35
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:24,752
Thank you.

36
00:01:24,775 --> 00:01:26,874
I'll take this one.

37
00:01:26,898 --> 00:01:28,831
Thank you.

38
00:01:28,854 --> 00:01:32,128
Can I pay with a card?

39
00:01:32,152 --> 00:01:34,190
Yes, you can.

40
00:01:34,213 --> 00:01:37,146
Then I'll pay by card, please.

41
00:01:37,169 --> 00:01:39,043
Thank you.

42
00:01:39,066 --> 00:01:41,700
That'll be 3,000 yen.

43
00:01:41,723 --> 00:01:50,732
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

44
00:01:50,732 --> 00:01:52,232
Scene 2: How to Choose What to Eat

45
00:01:52,232 --> 00:01:55,473
I'm hungry, aren't you?

46
00:01:55,496 --> 00:01:57,263
Yeah, I am.

47
00:01:57,286 --> 00:01:59,955
Let's grab something to eat.

48
00:01:59,978 --> 00:02:02,712
What do you feel like eating?

49
00:02:02,735 --> 00:02:06,379
I'm craving meat.

50
00:02:06,402 --> 00:02:10,202
How about that place over there?

51
00:02:10,225 --> 00:02:12,159
Sounds good!

52
00:02:12,182 --> 00:02:14,399
Let's go in.

53
00:02:14,422 --> 00:02:16,824
Could I see the menu, please?

54
00:02:16,847 --> 00:02:19,481
Sure, here you go.

55
00:02:19,504 --> 00:02:21,545
Thank you.

56
00:02:21,568 --> 00:02:24,501
I'll have the hamburger steak.

57
00:02:24,525 --> 00:02:27,725
Is the hamburger steak good?

58
00:02:27,748 --> 00:02:31,121
Yes, it's really delicious.

59
00:02:31,144 --> 00:02:35,144
Then I'll have the hamburger steak too.

60
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:38,201
What would you like to drink?

61
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:40,602
I'd like coffee, please.

62
00:02:40,626 --> 00:02:43,686
I'll have juice.

63
00:02:43,709 --> 00:02:45,591
Excuse me.

64
00:02:45,615 --> 00:02:48,015
Could we place our order, please?

65
00:02:48,038 --> 00:02:51,320
Two hamburger steaks, please.

66
00:02:51,343 --> 00:02:54,800
One coffee, please.

67
00:02:54,824 --> 00:02:57,831
And one juice, please.

68
00:02:57,855 --> 00:03:00,230
That's all.

69
00:03:00,253 --> 00:03:02,745
Is this your first time at this restaurant?

70
00:03:02,768 --> 00:03:05,604
Yes, it's my first time.

71
00:03:05,627 --> 00:03:08,274
I come here often.

72
00:03:08,297 --> 00:03:12,469
I see. Are the other dishes good too?

73
00:03:12,493 --> 00:03:16,293
Yes, the curry is delicious as well.

74
00:03:16,316 --> 00:03:19,401
I'd love to try the curry next time.

75
00:03:19,424 --> 00:03:21,024
Sounds good!

76
00:03:21,047 --> 00:03:23,186
Let's come again.

77
00:03:23,210 --> 00:03:25,902
Yes, let's do that.

78
00:03:25,925 --> 00:03:28,995
Oh, here comes our food!

79
00:03:29,019 --> 00:03:30,952
Let's dig in!

80
00:03:30,975 --> 00:03:38,080
The link to review today's video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

81
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,580
Scene 3: Buying a Laptop / A Conversation About Purchasing a Computer

82
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,428
Excuse me.

83
00:03:41,451 --> 00:03:44,101
Welcome! How can I help you?

84
00:03:44,124 --> 00:03:46,699
I'd like to look at some laptops.

85
00:03:46,723 --> 00:03:48,794
Laptops, sure.

86
00:03:48,818 --> 00:03:50,784
Right this way, please.

87
00:03:50,807 --> 00:03:52,690
Thank you.

88
00:03:52,713 --> 00:03:55,647
What kind of laptop are you looking for?

89
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:59,703
I want something light and compact.

90
00:03:59,726 --> 00:04:01,893
How about this one?

91
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:03,785
Sounds good!

92
00:04:03,808 --> 00:04:06,774
Where is this laptop made?

93
00:04:06,797 --> 00:04:09,633
It's made in Japan.

94
00:04:09,657 --> 00:04:11,324
I see.

95
00:04:11,347 --> 00:04:13,280
How much is it?

96
00:04:13,303 --> 00:04:15,672
It's 80,000 yen.

97
00:04:15,696 --> 00:04:18,302
That's a bit expensive.

98
00:04:18,326 --> 00:04:21,597
Then how about this one?

99
00:04:21,621 --> 00:04:23,387
How much is it?

100
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:25,781
It's 50,000 yen.

101
00:04:25,805 --> 00:04:27,573
That's a good price!

102
00:04:27,597 --> 00:04:30,930
Yes, it's very popular.

103
00:04:30,953 --> 00:04:33,608
Is it only available in black?

104
00:04:33,631 --> 00:04:37,465
No, we also have white and red.

105
00:04:37,488 --> 00:04:39,732
Can I see the red one?

106
00:04:39,755 --> 00:04:43,088
Sure, just a moment, please.

107
00:04:43,111 --> 00:04:44,682
Thank you.

108
00:04:44,706 --> 00:04:46,679
Sorry to keep you waiting.

109
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,436
Here's the red one.

110
00:04:48,459 --> 00:04:50,726
This red is so pretty!

111
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:54,482
Yes, it's very popular with students.

112
00:04:54,505 --> 00:04:57,072
How much does it weigh?

113
00:04:57,095 --> 00:04:59,728
About 1 kilogram.

114
00:04:59,751 --> 00:05:01,618
That's really light!

115
00:05:01,641 --> 00:05:03,094
Sounds good!

116
00:05:03,117 --> 00:05:04,917
I'll take this one.

117
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:07,236
Thank you.

118
00:05:07,259 --> 00:05:08,759
Scene 4: Ordering Practice / Practice for Placing Food Orders

119
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:10,892
Welcome!

120
00:05:10,915 --> 00:05:13,796
Can I get a hamburger, please?

121
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:16,862
Sure, one hamburger coming right up.

122
00:05:16,885 --> 00:05:21,218
And I'll take an order of fries, too.

123
00:05:21,241 --> 00:05:24,608
What size fries would you like?

124
00:05:24,631 --> 00:05:27,704
Small, please.

125
00:05:27,728 --> 00:05:29,895
Got it.

126
00:05:29,918 --> 00:05:32,852
Would you like anything to drink?

127
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:35,608
A Coke, please.

128
00:05:35,631 --> 00:05:38,598
Will that be a small Coke?

129
00:05:38,621 --> 00:05:42,954
No, medium, please.

130
00:05:42,977 --> 00:05:45,192
Got it.

131
00:05:45,215 --> 00:05:48,349
How much is that altogether?

132
00:05:48,372 --> 00:05:50,750
That'll be 600 yen.

133
00:05:50,773 --> 00:05:53,057
I'll eat here.

134
00:05:53,081 --> 00:05:54,681
Got it.

135
00:05:54,704 --> 00:05:57,271
Oh, excuse me.

136
00:05:57,293 --> 00:06:00,227
Yes? How can I help?

137
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:04,948
Actually, can I change the fries to a medium?

138
00:06:04,971 --> 00:06:07,138
Got it.

139
00:06:07,161 --> 00:06:09,494
Just a moment, please.

140
00:06:09,517 --> 00:06:11,484
Thank you.

141
00:06:11,507 --> 00:06:13,640
Sorry to keep you waiting.

142
00:06:13,663 --> 00:06:16,438
That'll be 700 yen.

143
00:06:16,462 --> 00:06:19,395
Here's 1000 yen.

144
00:06:19,418 --> 00:06:22,285
Your change is 300 yen.

145
00:06:22,308 --> 00:06:24,141
Thank you.

146
00:06:24,164 --> 00:06:26,180
Here's your receipt.

147
00:06:26,203 --> 00:06:27,937
Thanks.

148
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,605
You can wait for your order over there.

149
00:06:30,628 --> 00:06:33,195
Okay, got it.

150
00:06:33,218 --> 00:06:35,785
Thank you!

151
00:06:35,808 --> 00:06:37,308
Scene 5: Post-Graduation Plans

152
00:06:37,308 --> 00:06:40,519
We're graduating soon!

153
00:06:40,542 --> 00:06:42,676
Yeah, I am.

154
00:06:42,699 --> 00:06:45,265
Time really flew by, didn't it?

155
00:06:45,288 --> 00:06:49,222
What are your plans after graduation?

156
00:06:49,245 --> 00:06:52,978
I'm going to university.

157
00:06:53,001 --> 00:06:54,854
I see.

158
00:06:54,877 --> 00:06:57,911
What will you study?

159
00:06:57,934 --> 00:07:01,100
I'll study economics.

160
00:07:01,123 --> 00:07:03,690
Economics, huh?

161
00:07:03,713 --> 00:07:06,280
That sounds tough.

162
00:07:06,303 --> 00:07:08,352
Yeah, it is.

163
00:07:08,375 --> 00:07:12,242
But I'm studying for my future.

164
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:15,398
That's amazing!

165
00:07:15,421 --> 00:07:18,095
What about you?

166
00:07:18,119 --> 00:07:21,521
I'm going to work.

167
00:07:21,544 --> 00:07:24,678
Where will you work?

168
00:07:24,701 --> 00:07:28,107
At a travel agency.

169
00:07:28,130 --> 00:07:30,306
Sounds good!

170
00:07:30,329 --> 00:07:33,009
Do you like traveling?

171
00:07:33,033 --> 00:07:34,708
Yeah, it is.

172
00:07:34,732 --> 00:07:36,932
I love it!

173
00:07:36,955 --> 00:07:39,972
What kind of job will you do?

174
00:07:39,996 --> 00:07:43,083
I'll be a tour guide.

175
00:07:43,106 --> 00:07:45,342
That sounds fun!

176
00:07:45,365 --> 00:07:46,932
Yeah, it is.

177
00:07:46,955 --> 00:07:50,355
I want to meet people from all over the world.

178
00:07:50,378 --> 00:07:53,978
You're great at English, so that's perfect!

179
00:07:54,001 --> 00:07:55,640
Thank you.

180
00:07:55,663 --> 00:07:58,441
I'll study even harder.

181
00:07:58,465 --> 00:08:01,198
Let's both do our best!

182
00:08:01,221 --> 00:08:03,056
Yeah, it is.

183
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,046
Let's do our best!

184
00:08:05,069 --> 00:08:09,111
I'd love to visit your tour someday.

185
00:08:09,135 --> 00:08:11,421
Really?

186
00:08:11,444 --> 00:08:13,811
I'm so happy!

187
00:08:13,834 --> 00:08:16,685
Please show me around!

188
00:08:16,709 --> 00:08:18,709
Yeah, it is.

189
00:08:18,732 --> 00:08:21,024
I promise.

190
00:08:21,047 --> 00:08:24,022
I'm looking forward to it!

191
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:26,382
Thank you.

192
00:08:26,406 --> 00:08:27,906
Scene 6: Career Counseling and University Selection

193
00:08:27,906 --> 00:08:31,239
Excuse me, teacher. Do you have a moment?

194
00:08:31,262 --> 00:08:33,795
Yes, what is it?

195
00:08:33,818 --> 00:08:37,185
I'd like to discuss my future plans.

196
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:40,541
Sure, come this way.

197
00:08:40,564 --> 00:08:42,164
Thank you.

198
00:08:42,187 --> 00:08:44,121
Thank you.

199
00:08:44,144 --> 00:08:46,195
What's on your mind?

200
00:08:46,218 --> 00:08:48,985
I want to go to university.

201
00:08:49,008 --> 00:08:52,294
I see. Which university?

202
00:08:52,317 --> 00:08:55,483
I want to go to the University of Tokyo.

203
00:08:55,506 --> 00:08:59,673
The University of Tokyo? That's challenging.

204
00:08:59,696 --> 00:09:02,392
Yes, I know.

205
00:09:02,415 --> 00:09:05,015
What do you want to study?

206
00:09:05,038 --> 00:09:08,671
I want to study computer science.

207
00:09:08,694 --> 00:09:12,028
That's great. Are you good at math?

208
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:14,743
Yes, I like it.

209
00:09:14,766 --> 00:09:16,826
That's good to hear.

210
00:09:16,849 --> 00:09:20,416
But my Japanese isn't very good yet.

211
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:25,073
I see. You'll need to study more.

212
00:09:25,096 --> 00:09:29,168
Yes, I study for three hours every day.

213
00:09:29,191 --> 00:09:32,560
That's impressive. Keep it up!

214
00:09:32,583 --> 00:09:34,517
Thank you.

215
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:38,578
If you have any questions, feel free to ask anytime.

216
00:09:38,602 --> 00:09:40,977
Yes, I will. Thank you.

217
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,567
Good luck with your kanji tests too!

218
00:09:44,590 --> 00:09:47,724
Yes, I'll practice writing them every day.

219
00:09:47,746 --> 00:09:49,836
I'm rooting for you!

220
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,877
Thank you. I'll do my best!

221
00:09:52,901 --> 00:09:55,341
Alright, see you tomorrow.

222
00:09:55,365 --> 00:09:57,698
Yes, goodbye.

223
00:09:57,721 --> 00:09:59,221
Scene 7: Basics of a Job Interview

224
00:09:59,221 --> 00:10:01,555
Welcome!

225
00:10:01,579 --> 00:10:05,579
Um, I'm here for the part-time job interview.

226
00:10:05,602 --> 00:10:07,869
We've been expecting you.

227
00:10:07,892 --> 00:10:10,225
Right this way, please.

228
00:10:10,248 --> 00:10:11,854
Thank you.

229
00:10:11,877 --> 00:10:14,117
Please have a seat.

230
00:10:14,141 --> 00:10:15,811
Thank you.

231
00:10:15,835 --> 00:10:18,730
May I see your resume?

232
00:10:18,753 --> 00:10:21,286
Sure, here it is.

233
00:10:21,309 --> 00:10:22,978
Thank you.

234
00:10:23,001 --> 00:10:24,968
What's your name?

235
00:10:24,991 --> 00:10:28,287
I'm Ken.

236
00:10:28,310 --> 00:10:30,310
Ken, right?

237
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:32,200
Are you a student?

238
00:10:32,223 --> 00:10:36,263
Yes, I'm a student at a Japanese language school.

239
00:10:36,287 --> 00:10:39,554
When did you come to Japan?

240
00:10:39,577 --> 00:10:42,476
I came last April.

241
00:10:42,499 --> 00:10:43,995
I see.

242
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:46,553
Your Japanese is very good.

243
00:10:46,577 --> 00:10:48,218
Thank you.

244
00:10:48,241 --> 00:10:51,608
Do you have any part-time job experience?

245
00:10:51,631 --> 00:10:55,041
Yes, I used to work at a convenience store.

246
00:10:55,065 --> 00:10:56,903
I see.

247
00:10:56,926 --> 00:10:59,459
Is this your first time working at a restaurant?

248
00:10:59,482 --> 00:11:02,415
Yes, it's my first time.

249
00:11:02,438 --> 00:11:05,438
Can you cook?

250
00:11:05,461 --> 00:11:08,312
Yes, I can cook a little.

251
00:11:08,336 --> 00:11:11,586
Which days are you available to work?

252
00:11:11,609 --> 00:11:16,575
I can work on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays.

253
00:11:16,598 --> 00:11:19,676
What hours are you available?

254
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:23,033
From 5 PM to 10 PM.

255
00:11:23,056 --> 00:11:24,823
Got it.

256
00:11:24,846 --> 00:11:27,412
We’ll call you tomorrow with the results.

257
00:11:27,435 --> 00:11:30,602
Yes, thank you for your time.

258
00:11:30,625 --> 00:11:32,831
Thank you for today.

259
00:11:32,855 --> 00:11:34,525
Thank you!

260
00:11:34,549 --> 00:11:36,644
Thank you.

261
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,167
Scene 8: Exploring Temples in Kyoto

262
00:11:38,167 --> 00:11:42,611
I’d like to go somewhere this weekend.

263
00:11:42,635 --> 00:11:44,435
Sounds good!

264
00:11:44,458 --> 00:11:46,939
Where would you like to go?

265
00:11:46,962 --> 00:11:50,844
Do you know any good places?

266
00:11:50,868 --> 00:11:53,101
How about Kyoto?

267
00:11:53,124 --> 00:11:55,357
Kyoto?

268
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:57,150
Sounds good!

269
00:11:57,174 --> 00:12:00,909
There are so many historic temples there.

270
00:12:00,933 --> 00:12:03,899
I love visiting temples.

271
00:12:03,922 --> 00:12:07,722
Then I recommend Kiyomizu-dera.

272
00:12:07,745 --> 00:12:10,145
Kiyomizu-dera?

273
00:12:10,168 --> 00:12:12,368
What’s it like?

274
00:12:12,391 --> 00:12:16,084
It’s a very large and beautiful temple.

275
00:12:16,108 --> 00:12:19,875
Is it far?

276
00:12:19,898 --> 00:12:24,631
No, it’s only about 15 minutes by bus from the station.

277
00:12:24,654 --> 00:12:26,491
That’s close!

278
00:12:26,515 --> 00:12:30,768
Yes, and the view is amazing.

279
00:12:30,792 --> 00:12:34,025
I want to take lots of photos.

280
00:12:34,048 --> 00:12:37,581
In spring, the cherry blossoms are stunning.

281
00:12:37,604 --> 00:12:39,415
Sounds good!

282
00:12:39,439 --> 00:12:42,292
Is the food good there?

283
00:12:42,316 --> 00:12:47,083
Yes, the matcha ice cream is delicious.

284
00:12:47,106 --> 00:12:50,911
I love sweets!

285
00:12:50,934 --> 00:12:54,701
Then you should definitely try it.

286
00:12:54,724 --> 00:12:56,391
Got it.

287
00:12:56,414 --> 00:12:59,506
Any other recommendations?

288
00:12:59,530 --> 00:13:03,224
There are lots of souvenir shops too.

289
00:13:03,247 --> 00:13:05,913
I’d love to do some shopping.

290
00:13:05,936 --> 00:13:08,070
It’s a lot of fun.

291
00:13:08,093 --> 00:13:10,926
Thanks for the tips!

292
00:13:10,949 --> 00:13:14,482
You’re welcome. Have a great time!

293
00:13:14,505 --> 00:13:18,273
Yes, I’m really looking forward to the weekend.

294
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:21,589
Let me know how it goes!

295
00:13:21,613 --> 00:13:24,979
I definitely will.

296
00:13:25,002 --> 00:13:26,502
Scene 9: Asking for Directions

297
00:13:26,502 --> 00:13:28,707
Excuse me.

298
00:13:28,731 --> 00:13:31,535
Yes, how can I help you?

299
00:13:31,559 --> 00:13:33,734
I’m lost.

300
00:13:33,757 --> 00:13:36,090
Where are you trying to go?

301
00:13:36,113 --> 00:13:38,806
I need to get to the city hall.

302
00:13:38,830 --> 00:13:40,764
City hall, right?

303
00:13:40,787 --> 00:13:44,222
It's a 10-minute walk from here.

304
00:13:44,245 --> 00:13:46,578
How do I get there?

305
00:13:46,601 --> 00:13:49,934
Go straight down this road.

306
00:13:49,957 --> 00:13:52,095
Straight ahead, right?

307
00:13:52,119 --> 00:13:53,595
Yeah, it is.

308
00:13:53,619 --> 00:13:58,796
Then, take a right at the second traffic light.

309
00:13:58,819 --> 00:14:02,098
Right at the second traffic light, got it.

310
00:14:02,122 --> 00:14:04,455
That's right.

311
00:14:04,478 --> 00:14:09,097
You'll see a large white building on your left.

312
00:14:09,121 --> 00:14:11,854
A large white building, okay.

313
00:14:11,877 --> 00:14:13,410
Yeah, it is.

314
00:14:13,433 --> 00:14:15,967
That's the city hall.

315
00:14:15,990 --> 00:14:17,680
Got it.

316
00:14:17,704 --> 00:14:21,104
There's also a post office nearby.

317
00:14:21,127 --> 00:14:23,693
Next to the post office?

318
00:14:23,716 --> 00:14:25,483
Yeah, it is.

319
00:14:25,506 --> 00:14:28,202
To the right of the post office.

320
00:14:28,226 --> 00:14:30,118
Thank you.

321
00:14:30,142 --> 00:14:33,675
No, just be careful, okay?

322
00:14:33,698 --> 00:14:35,943
Oh, excuse me.

323
00:14:35,966 --> 00:14:37,933
Can I ask one more thing?

324
00:14:37,956 --> 00:14:39,323
Yeah, it is.

325
00:14:39,346 --> 00:14:41,004
Sure, what is it?

326
00:14:41,028 --> 00:14:44,482
Is there a convenience store nearby?

327
00:14:44,505 --> 00:14:45,574
Yeah, it is.

328
00:14:45,598 --> 00:14:48,410
There's one just around that corner.

329
00:14:48,433 --> 00:14:50,467
Oh, I see it!

330
00:14:50,491 --> 00:14:52,469
Thank you.

331
00:14:52,492 --> 00:14:55,949
Make sure to stay hydrated, okay?

332
00:14:55,973 --> 00:14:57,339
Yeah, it is.

333
00:14:57,362 --> 00:14:58,696
I will.

334
00:14:58,719 --> 00:15:00,565
Take care.

335
00:15:00,588 --> 00:15:02,855
Thank you!

336
00:15:12,886 --> 00:15:14,386
Scene 10: Meeting Up / Natural Japanese Conversation for Rendezvous

337
00:15:14,386 --> 00:15:18,435
Hello, where are you now?

338
00:15:18,458 --> 00:15:23,791
Hi, I'm in front of the station.

339
00:15:23,814 --> 00:15:26,481
At the north exit?

340
00:15:26,504 --> 00:15:28,537
Or the south exit?

341
00:15:28,561 --> 00:15:32,527
Uh, the north exit.

342
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:36,183
I'm at the south exit.

343
00:15:36,206 --> 00:15:39,973
I see. What should we do?

344
00:15:39,996 --> 00:15:42,863
I'll come to the north exit.

345
00:15:42,886 --> 00:15:46,019
Sorry about that, thanks!

346
00:15:46,042 --> 00:15:48,734
Wait for me there, okay?

347
00:15:48,758 --> 00:15:52,598
Sure, I'll be under the clock.

348
00:15:52,621 --> 00:15:55,872
Got it. I'll be right there.

349
00:15:55,895 --> 00:15:58,629
Please come carefully.

350
00:15:58,652 --> 00:16:01,985
Okay. Oh, I see you!

351
00:16:02,008 --> 00:16:04,697
Ah, there you are!

352
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,653
Sorry to keep you waiting.

353
00:16:06,676 --> 00:16:10,324
No, I just got here too.

354
00:16:10,348 --> 00:16:13,348
What time does the movie start?

355
00:16:13,371 --> 00:16:15,409
At 2:30.

356
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:18,267
We still have time, don't we?

357
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:21,969
Yeah. Should we grab lunch?

358
00:16:21,992 --> 00:16:23,725
Sounds good!

359
00:16:23,748 --> 00:16:26,081
What do you feel like eating?

360
00:16:26,104 --> 00:16:29,904
I'm craving ramen.

361
00:16:29,927 --> 00:16:33,497
There's a great ramen place nearby.

362
00:16:33,521 --> 00:16:35,054
Really?

363
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:36,731
Let's go!

364
00:16:36,754 --> 00:16:39,521
Sure, here it is.

365
00:16:39,544 --> 00:16:41,344
Is it crowded?

366
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:44,300
I think it's not too busy today.

367
00:16:44,323 --> 00:16:46,523
Great!

368
00:16:46,546 --> 00:16:49,152
Come on, let's hurry!

369
00:16:49,176 --> 00:16:50,589
Yeah, it is.

370
00:17:00,248 --> 00:17:01,748
Scene 1: The Basics of Customer Service

371
00:17:01,748 --> 00:17:04,086
Listening Test

372
00:17:04,086 --> 00:17:06,753
Excuse me.

373
00:17:06,753 --> 00:17:10,462
Excuse me / I'm sorry

374
00:17:10,485 --> 00:17:13,552
Listening Test

375
00:17:13,552 --> 00:17:17,101
Welcome! How can I help you?

376
00:17:17,101 --> 00:17:22,001
Welcome (to the store)

377
00:17:22,024 --> 00:17:25,542
Listening Test

378
00:17:25,542 --> 00:17:29,675
Could I see this shirt, please?

379
00:17:29,675 --> 00:17:35,375
Please do [V-te form] (e.g., Please show me = 見せてください)

380
00:17:35,398 --> 00:17:38,370
Listening Test

381
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:41,837
Of course, here you go.

382
00:17:41,837 --> 00:17:46,604
Here you are / Go ahead

383
00:17:46,627 --> 00:17:49,060
Listening Test

384
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,798
Thank you.

385
00:17:55,654 --> 00:17:58,691
Listening Test

386
00:17:58,691 --> 00:18:02,229
This looks really nice.

387
00:18:02,229 --> 00:18:07,129
It is [i-Adj], isn't it? (e.g., いいですね = It's good, isn't it?)

388
00:18:07,152 --> 00:18:11,223
Listening Test

389
00:18:11,223 --> 00:18:16,057
Yes, it's very popular.

390
00:18:16,057 --> 00:18:22,636
There is [N] / I have [N] (e.g., 人気があります = It's popular)

391
00:18:22,659 --> 00:18:25,492
Listening Test

392
00:18:25,492 --> 00:18:28,760
How much is it?

393
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:33,273
Is this [N]? (e.g., これはいくらですか = How much is this?)

394
00:18:33,296 --> 00:18:36,014
Listening Test

395
00:18:36,014 --> 00:18:39,148
It's 3,000 yen.

396
00:18:39,148 --> 00:18:43,481
It is [N] (e.g., 円です = It's [X] yen)

397
00:18:43,504 --> 00:18:45,672
Listening Test

398
00:18:45,672 --> 00:18:48,105
I see.

399
00:18:48,105 --> 00:18:51,540
I see / Is that so?

400
00:18:51,563 --> 00:18:54,755
Listening Test

401
00:18:54,755 --> 00:18:58,489
Do you have other colors?

402
00:18:58,489 --> 00:19:03,622
Do you have [N]? / Is there [N]? (e.g., 他の色はありますか = Do you have other colors?)

403
00:19:03,645 --> 00:19:07,431
Listening Test

404
00:19:07,431 --> 00:19:11,898
Yes, we have white and black.

405
00:19:11,898 --> 00:19:18,005
[N1] and [N2] (e.g., 白と黒 = white and black)

406
00:19:18,028 --> 00:19:20,928
Listening Test

407
00:19:20,928 --> 00:19:24,262
Could I see the white one, please?

408
00:19:24,262 --> 00:19:28,861
Please show me [N] (e.g., [N]を見せてください)

409
00:19:28,884 --> 00:19:31,917
Listening Test

410
00:19:31,917 --> 00:19:35,417
Sure, here it is.

411
00:19:35,417 --> 00:19:40,250
This way / Here

412
00:19:40,273 --> 00:19:42,707
Listening Test

413
00:19:42,707 --> 00:19:45,480
It's beautiful.

414
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:49,346
It is [na-Adj], isn't it? (e.g., きれいですね = It's beautiful, isn't it?)

415
00:19:49,369 --> 00:19:52,757
Listening Test

416
00:19:52,757 --> 00:19:56,725
What size is this?

417
00:19:56,725 --> 00:20:02,192
How many? / What size? (e.g., サイズはいくつですか = What size is it?)

418
00:20:02,215 --> 00:20:04,793
Listening Test

419
00:20:04,793 --> 00:20:07,740
It's a medium.

420
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:11,840
It is [N]

421
00:20:11,863 --> 00:20:14,767
Listening Test

422
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:18,134
Do you have a large size?

423
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:22,768
Do you have [N]? / Is there [N]?

424
00:20:22,791 --> 00:20:25,625
Listening Test

425
00:20:25,625 --> 00:20:28,891
Yes, we do.

426
00:20:28,891 --> 00:20:33,391
There is / We have

427
00:20:33,414 --> 00:20:36,398
Listening Test

428
00:20:36,398 --> 00:20:39,865
Just a moment, please.

429
00:20:39,865 --> 00:20:44,632
Please do [V-masu stem] (polite) (e.g., 少々お待ちください = Please wait a moment)

430
00:20:44,655 --> 00:20:46,755
Listening Test

431
00:20:46,755 --> 00:20:49,106
Thank you.

432
00:20:49,106 --> 00:20:52,407
Please (request)

433
00:20:52,431 --> 00:20:54,864
Listening Test

434
00:20:54,864 --> 00:20:57,601
Sorry to keep you waiting.

435
00:20:57,601 --> 00:21:01,435
Thank you for waiting

436
00:21:01,458 --> 00:21:03,958
Listening Test

437
00:21:03,958 --> 00:21:06,824
Here's the large size.

438
00:21:06,824 --> 00:21:10,783
It is [N]

439
00:21:10,806 --> 00:21:13,573
Listening Test

440
00:21:13,573 --> 00:21:16,755
May I try it on?

441
00:21:16,755 --> 00:21:21,151
May I do [V-te form]? (e.g., 着てもいいですか = May I try this on?)

442
00:21:21,175 --> 00:21:24,689
Listening Test

443
00:21:24,689 --> 00:21:28,805
Of course, the fitting room is over there.

444
00:21:28,805 --> 00:21:34,472
Please go to [N] / This way, please (e.g., あちらへどうぞ = This way, please)

445
00:21:34,495 --> 00:21:36,832
Listening Test

446
00:21:36,832 --> 00:21:39,498
Thank you.

447
00:21:43,221 --> 00:21:45,572
Listening Test

448
00:21:45,572 --> 00:21:48,239
How does it look?

449
00:21:48,239 --> 00:21:51,957
How is it? / How does it look?

450
00:21:51,981 --> 00:21:54,695
Listening Test

451
00:21:54,695 --> 00:21:57,828
It fits perfectly.

452
00:21:57,828 --> 00:22:02,137
Perfectly [i-Adj] / Just right (e.g., ちょうどいい = just right)

453
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:04,827
Listening Test

454
00:22:04,827 --> 00:22:07,894
It really suits you!

455
00:22:07,894 --> 00:22:12,132
Do [V] well (e.g., よく似合います = It suits you well)

456
00:22:12,155 --> 00:22:14,523
Listening Test

457
00:22:14,523 --> 00:22:17,223
Thank you.

458
00:22:20,993 --> 00:22:23,529
Listening Test

459
00:22:23,529 --> 00:22:26,430
I'll take this one.

460
00:22:26,430 --> 00:22:30,464
I will [V] this (e.g., これを買います = I'll buy this)

461
00:22:30,486 --> 00:22:32,870
Listening Test

462
00:22:32,870 --> 00:22:35,604
Thank you.

463
00:22:39,421 --> 00:22:43,055
Listening Test

464
00:22:43,055 --> 00:22:47,321
Can I pay with a card?

465
00:22:47,321 --> 00:22:53,155
Can you do [V-dictionary form]? (e.g., カードで払うことができますか = Can I pay by card?)

466
00:22:53,178 --> 00:22:55,678
Listening Test

467
00:22:55,678 --> 00:22:58,517
Yes, you can.

468
00:22:58,517 --> 00:23:02,451
Can do / Possible

469
00:23:02,475 --> 00:23:05,749
Listening Test

470
00:23:05,749 --> 00:23:09,582
Then I'll pay by card, please.

471
00:23:09,582 --> 00:23:14,849
By [N], please (e.g., じゃあ、カードでお願いします = Then, by card, please)

472
00:23:14,872 --> 00:23:17,213
Listening Test

473
00:23:17,213 --> 00:23:19,879
Thank you.

474
00:23:23,613 --> 00:23:26,646
Listening Test

475
00:23:26,646 --> 00:23:30,154
That'll be 3,000 yen.

476
00:23:30,154 --> 00:23:35,021
It will be [N] / That comes to [N]

477
00:23:35,044 --> 00:23:36,544
Scene 2: How to Choose What to Eat

478
00:23:36,544 --> 00:23:40,116
Listening Test

479
00:23:40,116 --> 00:23:44,312
I'm hungry, aren't you?

480
00:23:44,312 --> 00:23:50,070
To become hungry

481
00:23:50,094 --> 00:23:52,327
Listening Test

482
00:23:52,327 --> 00:23:54,846
Yeah, I am.

483
00:23:58,385 --> 00:24:01,452
Listening Test

484
00:24:01,452 --> 00:24:05,019
Let's grab something to eat.

485
00:24:05,019 --> 00:24:09,922
Something to eat (e.g., 何か食べたい = I want to eat something)

486
00:24:09,946 --> 00:24:13,060
Listening Test

487
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:16,693
What do you feel like eating?

488
00:24:16,693 --> 00:24:21,682
Want to do [V] (e.g., 食べたい = want to eat)

489
00:24:21,705 --> 00:24:25,643
Listening Test

490
00:24:25,643 --> 00:24:30,310
I'm craving meat.

491
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:36,680
Want to [V] [N] (e.g., 肉が食べたい = I want to eat meat)

492
00:24:36,704 --> 00:24:40,780
Listening Test

493
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:45,613
How about that place over there?

494
00:24:45,613 --> 00:24:52,211
How about [N]? (e.g., このお店はどうですか = How about this restaurant?)

495
00:24:52,234 --> 00:24:54,616
Listening Test

496
00:24:54,616 --> 00:24:57,319
Sounds good!

497
00:24:57,319 --> 00:25:01,086
Good ↔ Bad

498
00:25:01,110 --> 00:25:03,746
Listening Test

499
00:25:03,746 --> 00:25:06,779
Let's go in.

500
00:25:06,779 --> 00:25:11,012
Let's do [V] (e.g., 入りましょう = Let's go in)

501
00:25:11,035 --> 00:25:13,869
Listening Test

502
00:25:13,869 --> 00:25:17,135
Could I see the menu, please?

503
00:25:17,135 --> 00:25:21,648
Please do [V-te form] (e.g., 見せてください = Please show me)

504
00:25:21,672 --> 00:25:24,705
Listening Test

505
00:25:24,705 --> 00:25:28,211
Sure, here you go.

506
00:25:28,211 --> 00:25:33,078
Please / Here you go

507
00:25:33,101 --> 00:25:35,601
Listening Test

508
00:25:35,601 --> 00:25:38,468
Thank you.

509
00:25:42,427 --> 00:25:45,727
Listening Test

510
00:25:45,727 --> 00:25:49,594
I'll have the hamburger steak.

511
00:25:49,594 --> 00:25:54,927
I'll decide on [N] (e.g., ハンバーグにする = I'll have the hamburg steak)

512
00:25:54,950 --> 00:25:58,484
Listening Test

513
00:25:58,484 --> 00:26:02,618
Is the hamburger steak good?

514
00:26:02,618 --> 00:26:08,331
Is it [i-Adj]? (e.g., おいしいですか = Is it delicious?)

515
00:26:08,354 --> 00:26:12,054
Listening Test

516
00:26:12,054 --> 00:26:16,393
Yes, it's really delicious.

517
00:26:16,393 --> 00:26:22,374
Very [i-Adj] (e.g., とてもおいしい = very delicious)

518
00:26:22,398 --> 00:26:26,664
Listening Test

519
00:26:26,664 --> 00:26:31,698
Then I'll have the hamburger steak too.

520
00:26:31,698 --> 00:26:38,575
[N] too / also (e.g., コーヒーも = coffee too)

521
00:26:38,598 --> 00:26:41,976
Listening Test

522
00:26:41,976 --> 00:26:45,943
What would you like to drink?

523
00:26:45,943 --> 00:26:51,409
I'll decide on [N] (e.g., 飲み物にする = I'll have a drink)

524
00:26:51,432 --> 00:26:54,218
Listening Test

525
00:26:54,218 --> 00:26:57,452
I'd like coffee, please.

526
00:26:57,452 --> 00:27:01,918
[N] is good / I prefer [N] (e.g., コーヒーがいい = I prefer coffee)

527
00:27:01,941 --> 00:27:05,337
Listening Test

528
00:27:05,337 --> 00:27:09,308
I'll have juice.

529
00:27:09,308 --> 00:27:14,808
I'll decide on [N] (e.g., ジュースにする = I'll have juice)

530
00:27:14,831 --> 00:27:17,173
Listening Test

531
00:27:17,173 --> 00:27:19,840
Excuse me.

532
00:27:23,564 --> 00:27:26,397
Listening Test

533
00:27:26,397 --> 00:27:29,664
Could we place our order, please?

534
00:27:29,664 --> 00:27:34,164
Please give me [N] (e.g., 注文をお願いします = Please take my order)

535
00:27:34,187 --> 00:27:37,820
Listening Test

536
00:27:37,820 --> 00:27:42,087
Two hamburger steaks, please.

537
00:27:42,087 --> 00:27:47,920
N + を + [number] + お願いします = Please give me [number] of N
Example: 二つ = two things

538
00:27:47,943 --> 00:27:51,710
Listening Test

539
00:27:51,710 --> 00:27:56,176
One coffee, please.

540
00:27:56,176 --> 00:28:02,248
N + を + [number] + お願いします = Please give me [number] of N
Example: 一つ = one thing

541
00:28:02,272 --> 00:28:05,639
Listening Test

542
00:28:05,639 --> 00:28:09,572
And one juice, please.

543
00:28:09,572 --> 00:28:14,967
N + を + [number] + お願いします = Please give me [number] of N

544
00:28:14,991 --> 00:28:17,789
Listening Test

545
00:28:17,789 --> 00:28:21,022
That's all.

546
00:28:21,022 --> 00:28:25,489
以上です = That’s all.
Note: 以上 (more than/that’s all) ↔ 以下 (less than)

547
00:28:25,512 --> 00:28:28,412
Listening Test

548
00:28:28,412 --> 00:28:31,761
Is this your first time at this restaurant?

549
00:28:31,761 --> 00:28:36,394
初めて = for the first time
Note: 初めて (first time) ↔ 再び (again)

550
00:28:36,417 --> 00:28:39,650
Listening Test

551
